Package: spark-runtime
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCHITECTURE@
Maintainer: SparkPilot <feedback@sparkpilot.dev>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://example.invalid/spark-runtime
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.36), adduser, systemd, util-linux, sqlite3, nftables, python3, docker.io | docker-ce, docker-buildx | docker-buildx-plugin, nvidia-container-toolkit, network-manager, iproute2
Recommends: iputils-arping, iputils-ping, bluez, rfkill, git, fwupd
Description: Spark Runtime control service for NVIDIA DGX Spark
 Spark Runtime turns a DGX Spark into an appliance the SparkPilot Apple
 applications can discover, pair with, monitor, and use. It installs two
 services: sparkd, the unprivileged control daemon that serves the local
 HTTPS API and advertises the node over Bonjour, and spark-privd, a minimal
 root helper that accepts only typed, allowlisted operations over a
 Unix-domain socket.
 .
 The package ships no model weights, no credentials, and no generated state.
 A node identity and database are created by the postinst on first install
 and are never replaced by a later one. sqlite3 is a hard dependency: an
 upgrade takes a consistent database snapshot with it and refuses to proceed
 without one, because copying the database and its write-ahead log as separate
 files produces a snapshot whose halves can disagree.
 .
 LAB AND DEVELOPMENT USE. This build is not a production release and its
 trust root says so: the shipped release keys are scoped to the dev and lab
 channels, and a beta or stable manifest is refused by that shipped root.
 Schema-2 offline-root delegation and root-owned node authority delivered
 through read-only systemd credentials are implemented. Production release
 root enrollment and physical acceptance are still required before beta or
 stable qualification. Development invocations outside the packaged service
 retain explicit service-account file storage for local tests and tooling.
